# .env.production: the ONE env file git keeps (see .gitignore's exception).
# Public flags only, never a secret: Next.js bakes NEXT_PUBLIC_ values from
# this file into a production build, and scripts/verify_sample_switch.ts
# (plan step 48, 2026-09-19) reads it in the prebuild chain.
#
# THE SITE IS PRIVATE. He is the only reader (his 2026-09-11 switch hides the
# sample marks), so the marks stay off while this line stands. LAUNCH DAY:
# delete the private line and add NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_SAMPLE_MARKS=1, in one
# commit; the sample-switch gate fails a build that does one without the other.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_PRIVATE=1
